## Oracle finding

Pinned Java `ProcessQueue.fillProcessQueueInfo` catches and logs the
NullPointerException raised for a null info DTO, releases its read lock, and
returns normally. Rust now exposes `fill_process_queue_info_nullable`; present
values use the existing fill method and `None` is a no-op.

The invoked Java facade fixture records a normal return for a null DTO. Rust's
facade comparison calls the nullable adapter. Fixture SHA-256:
`57e2890ebeace93ecf00e2509e2bf7557c28f681ad19141f81430fecfe57ddf3`.

